 ],
 "caption_en": "The first one took 11 minutes. The rest is still being counted.\n\n14 May 1948: Israel's leaders sign the Declaration of Independence in Tel Aviv. At midnight Tel Aviv time (6 pm in Washington) the British Mandate ends and the state is born. 11 minutes later, the United States recognises it (de facto). 17 May 1948: the Soviet Union gives the first full legal (de jure) recognition.\n\nEnd of 1948: 17 countries. By 1950: 47. The 1960s: dozens of newly independent African states. 1979: Egypt, the first Arab country. The 1990s: about 40 more as the Soviet Union breaks up, including China (1992) and Jordan (1994). 2020: the UAE, Bahrain and Morocco (and Bhutan).\n\nToday: 169 of the other 192 UN members. 23 do not: Afghanistan, Algeria, Bangladesh, Brunei, Comoros, Djibouti, Indonesia, Iran, Iraq, Kuwait, Lebanon, Libya, Malaysia, North Korea, Oman, Pakistan, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, Somalia, Sudan, Syria, Tunisia, Yemen. These are governments' decisions, not peoples'.\n\nRecognising is not agreeing: many of them criticise Israel too, and some have cut ties and restored them over the years.\n\nWhich one surprised you?\n\nSources: US National Archives, \"U.S. Recognition of the State of Israel\" (11 minutes); Wikipedia, International recognition of Israel (Feb 2026). Photos: Eliezer Kaplan signs the Declaration, 1948, Zoltan Kluger, GPO (PD); Eliahu Epstein's letter to President Truman, 14 May 1948, Truman Library (PD); Sadat, Carter and Begin at the Camp David Accords, 1978, the road to the 1979 treaty (PD); Abraham Accords signing, 2020, White House (PD). Map: Natural Earth (PD). Made with AI tools, AI voice (Noam's cloned voice).",
 "caption_he": "מי הכיר בישראל ראשונה? ארצות הברית, 11 דקות אחרי שהמדינה קמה (הכרה בפועל). שלושה ימים אחר כך, ברית המועצות נתנה את ההכרה המשפטית המלאה הראשונה.\nסוף 1948: 17 מדינות. 1950: 47. 1979: מצרים, המדינה הערבית הראשונה. שנות ה 90: עוד כ 40, כולל סין וירדן. 2020: איחוד האמירויות, בחריין ומרוקו.\nהיום: 169 מתוך 192 חברות האו\"ם האחרות. 23 עדיין לא מכירות. הכרה היא לא הסכמה.",
